Decommit J3-30,31,32; note that the wires to J3-10,11,12 are removed.  Old
	IOBs run these wires indirectly through J11; for these, remove both
	wires.

;	Delete			Add
;
;	A27-5  : A27-6		E30-7  : E30-8  KBDIN-
;	A27-4  : J3-12		E30-17 : E30-16 -DATA BITS & -KBD CLK
;	C25-14 : J3-11		E30-3  : E30-4  KBDCLK+
;	C25-11 : J3-10		E30-5  : E30-6  KBDCLK-
;				E30-20 : E30-18 (power)
;				E30-12 : E30-14 ************ changed by ECO #9
;				D24-11 : E30-15 HI 3
;				E30-14 : E30-15 ************ changed by ECO #8
;				C25-14 : E30-16 (-DATA BITS & -KBD CLK from a nand gate
;					         in rev 4 and earlier, but not in rev 6:
;						 see 5/79 wirelist)
;				A27-6  : E30-13 -KBDIN
;				F30-20 : F30-18 (power)
;				F30-17 : F30-16 AUDIO
;				C25-11 : F30-16 AUDIO
;				F30-3  : F30-4  AUDIO-
;				F30-5  : F30-6  AUDIO+
;				E30-12 : F30-15 HI 3
;				E30-11 : E30-19 KBDIN RC
;				E30-2  : E30-10 (ground to RC capacitor)
;
Then add twisted pair as follows:		

;				J3-12 : E30-9, J3-32 : E30-7
;				J3-11 : E30-5, J3-31 : E30-4 ****** see note on eco #9
;				J3-10 : F30-5, J3-30 : F30-4

Note: The keyboard connector wiring must be consistent with the console keyboard
      connector wiring.  This is outlined in the console cable documentation.
      The above can be used in single ended mode by supplying a 1volt bias
      to J3-31 (-CLOCK) at either the IOB end or the keyboard end.
--------
;ECO#7  11/21/80  Moon	Speed up IOB clock to 8 microseconds per bit.
;			This is for use with the new, new keyboard which
;			has the mouse plugged into it.  Note, this ECO
;			will cause the machine not to work with the older
;			version of the Space Cadet keyboard.
;			All but the last line of this ECO simply undoes ECO#3.
;
;Signal			Delete			Add
;
;1 USEC CLK		F23-4 : C21-17		F23-4 : D24-4
;						D24-4 : C21-17
;
;TOD2			D24-4 : F23-8
;
;%C25-4			D24-13 : C25-4		D24-14 : C25-4
;-------
;ECO#8	1/31/81	RG,JLK	Fix typo in ECO#6
;Signal			Delete			Add
;			E30-14 : E30-15		E30-14 : E30-13
;
;ECO#9 5/13/81 RG,DRP another typo found in eco #6
;			delete			add
;			E30-12 : E30-14	       	E30-15 : E30-12
;					
;	ALSO: the sense of the KBDCLK+/KBDCLK- output of the 75118 differential
;	      driver at E30 on old IOBs is opposite that of new IOBs.  Therefore
;	      the twisted pair must be wired oppositely such that pin J3-11 has
;	      a red wire on it and has a logical one on it in the ready state.
;	      The symptom of of this potential bug is total lossage because the
;	      kbd micro will send no characters unless it sees a high clock signal.
;	      The wiring specified in eco#6 is correct for boards made from the
;	      12/79 wirelist (rev 4) and earlier.  I'm not sure about rev 5,
;	      because I don't have a copy.  Rev 6 (12/80) uses the wiring specified
;	      in the consolidation of 2/18/81 below. When in doubt, use the scope.
;

2/18/81  Consolidation: the additions currently necessary for a new IOB follow:

Decommit pins J3-23,30,31,32

Add twisted pairs as follows: +video     FH1 : J3-3  (red)
                              -video     FH2 : J3-23 (white)
                              
                                       E30-9 : J3-12 (red)
                                       E30-7 : J3-32 (white)
                                       
                                       E30-4 : J3-11 (red)
                                       E30-5 : J3-31 (white)

                                       F30-5 : J3-10 (red)
                                       F30-4 : J3-30 (white)

then add 6 jumpers to set timing:
  				       B3-5 : B3-6      ;these two determine transmit
				       B3-6 : B3-10     ;clock speed

				       B4-8 : B4-11     ;taps TD100 at 100 ns
				       B11-6 : B11-13    ;taps TD100 at 60 ns
				       A11-6 : A11-13    ;taps TD25 at 15 ns
				       A11-7 : A11-8     ;taps TD25 at 10 ns


ECO #10	12/13/81 Moon  	Output interrupts from 2651 for system 78.14
Enables interupts on output for serial I/O.

Add wire from A12-8 to C20-1.  Apply this only to IOB's wired for a 2651
on an adaptor at A12.  Install whether or not a 2651 is actually present,
although it makes no difference unless one is present.

ECO #11 12/81 DRP	Separate High run for 9401 crc chips. observed to be noise
			sensitive in some boards.

delete			add

			1K resistor from pin 1 to pin 20 of C09
A09-12 : C09-5		C09-1 : C09-5
C09-5 : C07-13		C09-5 :C07-13
C07-13 : D06-13		D06-13 : A09-12

ECO #12 12/81 DRP	Increase duty cycle of "fclk" and "-fclk" to 50%
			Makes timing on crc chips less marginal

delete			add

			74S04 in E15
BO3-17 : B05-4		B03-15 : B05-4 	;new source of fclk
D03-4 : D08-6		B03-15 :D08-6
D03-5 : B03-11		D03-5 : B03-11	;Carry still used to reset counter
			A08-11 : E15-8  ;invert fclk
B03-11 : A09-3		E15-9 : A09-3	;
			E15-17 : E15-20 ;power for S04
E03-12 :D03-5		A09-3 : E03-12